===Verb===
{{en-verb|4=joined,joint<q:archaic>}}

# {{senseid|en|combine}}{{lb|en|transitive}} To [[connect]] or [[combine]] into one; to put together.
#: {{ux|en|The plumber '''joined''' the two ends of the broken pipe.}}
#: {{ux|en|We '''joined''' our efforts to get an even better result.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To come together; to meet.
#: {{ux|en|Parallel lines never '''join'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|These two rivers '''join''' in about 80 miles.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To enter into [[association]] or [[alliance]], to [[unite]] in a [[common]] [[purpose]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=26|passage=Forſake thy king and do but '''ioyne''' with me<br>And we will triumph ouer al the world.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King John|act=3|scene=i|page=8|column=2|passage={{...}}Nature and Fortune '''ioyn’d''' to make thee great.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To start working on or participating in a project.
#: {{ux|en|He '''joined''' season 2 of the television show.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To come into the [[company]] of.
#: {{ux|en|I will '''join''' you in watching the football game as soon as I have finished my work.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|IV|46|No matter how early I came down, I would find him on the veranda, smoking cigarettes, or otherwise his man would be there with a message to say that his master would shortly '''join''' me if I would kindly wait.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To become a [[member]] of.
#: {{ux|en|Many children '''join''' a sports club.}}
#: {{ux|en|Most politicians have '''joined''' a party.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=22|passage=In the autumn there was a row at some cement works about the unskilled labour men. A union had just been started for them and all but a few '''joined'''. One of these blacklegs was laid for by a picket and knocked out of time.}}
